Here are the four layers of the Memo entity's shape definition, with exact file paths:

---

**1. SQL Schema**
`/bench/repo/store/migration/sqlite/LATEST.sql` -- line 33

```sql
CREATE TABLE memo (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  uid TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
  creator_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
  created_ts BIGINT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%s', 'now')),
  updated_ts BIGINT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%s', 'now')),
  row_status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (row_status IN ('NORMAL', 'ARCHIVED')) DEFAULT 'NORMAL',
  content TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
  visibility TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (visibility IN ('PUBLIC', 'PROTECTED', 'PRIVATE')) DEFAULT 'PRIVATE',
  pinned INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (pinned IN (0, 1)) DEFAULT 0,
  payload TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'
);
```
Columns: `id`, `uid`, `creator_id`, `created_ts`, `updated_ts`, `row_status`, `content`, `visibility`, `pinned`, `payload`. Equivalent schemas also exist at `/bench/repo/store/migration/postgres/LATEST.sql` and `/bench/repo/store/migration/mysql/LATEST.sql`.

---

**2. Go Store Model**
`/bench/repo/store/memo.go` -- line 35

```go
type Memo struct {
    ID        int32
    UID       string
    RowStatus RowStatus
    CreatorID int32
    CreatedTs int64
    UpdatedTs int64
    Content    string
    Visibility Visibility
    Pinned     bool
    Payload    *storepb.MemoPayload
    ParentUID *string
}
```
Fields map closely to the SQL columns, with `Payload` deserialized into a typed protobuf struct (`storepb.MemoPayload`) and an additional composed field `ParentUID`.

---

**3. API Proto Message**
`/bench/repo/proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto` -- line 198

```protobuf
message Memo {
  string name = 1;
  State state = 2;
  string creator = 3;
  google.protobuf.Timestamp create_time = 4;
  google.protobuf.Timestamp update_time = 5;
  string content = 7;
  Visibility visibility = 9;
  repeated string tags = 10;
  bool pinned = 11;
  repeated Attachment attachments = 12;
  repeated MemoRelation relations = 13;
  repeated Reaction reactions = 14;
  Property property = 15;
  optional string parent = 16;
  string snippet = 17;
  optional Location location = 18;
}
```
This is the API-facing representation. It uses resource names (`memos/{memo}`, `users/{user}`) instead of raw integer IDs, timestamps instead of unix epochs, and includes enriched output-only fields like `tags`, `reactions`, `property`, `snippet`, and `parent`.

There is also a separate store-level proto `Memo` message at `/bench/repo/proto/store/memo.proto` (line 435 match) and an additional `Memo` reference in `/bench/repo/proto/store/inbox.proto`.

---

